From 33cef66db1e510b214a17c5a616480720e706538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:43:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 097/105] consensus: deploy P2MR leaf version 0xe2 with lattice
 tripwire outputs, inactive on Ark-0

A buried deployment, p2mr_lattice_tripwire, the last of the buried
deployments, sets SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE on blocks at or above
its height where P2MR is active too, so that P2MR leaves of leaf version
0xe2 execute there. Next to its height, P2MRLatticeTripwireHeight, the
consensus parameters gain the lattice tripwire outputs,
p2mr_lattice_tripwires: from that height on, validation is to fail
OP_CHECKMLDSA44 checks in those leaves in every block whose parent leaves
one of them missing, which a later commit in this series implements. An
output is present while it is unspent and was created below that height.

- On the Ark-0 signet the height and the three outputs are rules of that
  network, ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT and ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_OUTPOINTS,
  each output with the SHA256 of the ML-DSA-44 key its leaf checks and a
  label. Neither is decided yet: the height is
  std::numeric_limits<int>::max() and the list is empty, so this build does
  not activate the rules on Ark-0, and leaf version 0xe2 stays an unknown
  leaf version there, as 0xe0 did before its height was set; a node there
  says so at startup. A commit of its own will set both, with the creation
  height of the outputs, once they are confirmed below the height. Static
  asserts keep the height above those of OP_CHECKMLDSA44 and of the
  tripwire rules of leaf version 0xe0, and at or above that of
  OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S. They also tie the height to the outputs as M3's
  constants do: while it is never, there is no creation height and no
  output; once it is finite, a creation height below it and exactly
  three distinct outputs with non-null txids, labelled "NUMS ML-DSA-44",
  "destroyed key" and "drill", the first with the NUMS key. The outputs
  are a constant array, ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRES, so that all of it is
  checked at compile time.
- The NUMS key of the first output is fixed by its construction: the domain
  separation tag "MLDSA44-NUMS/v1", the label "lattice-tripwire/0", and the
  SHA256 of the key, 591dae31...92805, which a unit test computes again.
- Another custom signet gets the rules only from
  -signetlatticetripwire=<height>@<txid:vout>[,<txid:vout>...], which needs
  -signetchallenge, -signetmldsa44, -signettripwire and -signetslhdsa128s,
  with the heights of the tripwire rules and of OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S at or
  below its own (and that of OP_CHECKMLDSA44 below the tripwire's, as
  -signettripwire already requires). The Ark-0 and the default signet
  refuse it. An outpoint with a null txid is refused: no output has it,
  and every coinbase input names it. -signettripwire keeps its syntax.
- Regtest activates leaf version 0xe2 where OP_CHECKMLDSA44, leaf version
  0xe0 and OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S are all active, without lattice tripwire outputs,
  unless -testactivationheight=p2mr_lattice_tripwire@N moves it.
  -signetlatticetripwire works there too and then sets the height, which
  must not also be given by -testactivationheight. Whatever sets it, a
  node refuses to start when the final height is below the final height
  of p2mr_mldsa44, p2mr_tripwire or p2mr_slhdsa128s: the mempool's removals
  below the heights of the two opcodes look at leaf versions 0xc0 and 0xe0
  only, and a spend of leaf version 0xe2 accepted above them would
  otherwise stay in the mempool after a reorganization below them.
- Mainnet, testnet3, testnet4 and the default signet never activate it. A
  node refuses to start with -signetlatticetripwire on a chain it is not
  for, whatever its value.

ValidDeployment now names DEPLOYMENT_P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE as the last
buried deployment. getdeploymentinfo reports the deployment, and a signet or
regtest node with lattice tripwire rules logs the height and the outputs at
startup: the outpoints, and for those the code fixes their label and the
SHA256 of their key. The startup line of OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S names leaf
version 0xe2 among the leaf versions it executes in where the deployment
is enabled. feature_p2mr_slhdsa128s.py, whose regtest node now executes
leaf version 0xe2 from the height of OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S, expects that line.
